        content: 'Generic small business tools do not understand that an irrigation system is a physical asset with zones, heads, and controllers that must be documented. Irrigation business software stores a system profile for every property, including zone diagrams, controller programming, and backflow test dates. When a sprinkler head breaks in July, the dispatcher already knows the model and the technician arrives with the right part. That asset history is the difference between a tool built for irrigation and a calendar app you forced to fit. A purpose fit platform also understands the seasonal cadence of the trade, the legal requirements around backflow certification, and the way a single property can carry a dozen separate zones each with its own flow rate and head count. Generic software treats every job as a blank appointment, while irrigation focused software treats every job as the next chapter in the documented life of a system you already know.',
