        content: 'Smart reputation tools can gauge customer sentiment before publicly steering anyone toward a review site. A delighted customer is pointed straight to your public profile to share praise, while a customer who signals frustration is invited to send feedback privately first so you can resolve the problem before it ever becomes a one star post. This routing protects your public rating while still surfacing the issues you genuinely need to fix, such as a missed appointment window or a zone that was overlooked. Catching dissatisfaction privately is every bit as valuable as gathering public praise, because it gives you the chance to send a tech back, make it right, and often convert an unhappy homeowner into a loyal advocate. The software handles this branching automatically based on how the customer responds.',
