        h2: 'Connecting Parts to Job Costing',
        content: 'Every part logged in the field flows directly into the job cost for that specific work, so the software knows exactly what materials each job consumed rather than relying on a rough after the fact estimate. Combined with the labor hours your tech records on the same visit, this gives you true job profitability instead of a hopeful guess scribbled at quote time. Tying parts directly to job costing means you can clearly see when a particular install used far more materials than you bid for, perhaps because the site needed extra valves or longer wire runs, and then adjust your future bids on similar properties accordingly. Accurate parts data captured at the point of use is absolutely essential to genuinely understanding which jobs and which job types are actually making you money.',
